1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,271
The Shoes-Off Question.

3
00:00:03,271 --> 00:00:05,635
Emma invites me over after school.

4
00:00:05,635 --> 00:00:09,823
I've met her at the park and the library, but this is my first visit to her house.

5
00:00:09,823 --> 00:00:13,583
At the front door, I notice several pairs of shoes lined up neatly.

6
00:00:13,583 --> 00:00:15,521
Should I take my shoes off?

7
00:00:15,746 --> 00:00:16,738
Yes, please.

8
00:00:16,738 --> 00:00:18,258
We usually leave them here.

9
00:00:18,258 --> 00:00:21,071
There are clean slippers in that basket if you'd like a pair.

10
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:22,521
Thanks.

11
00:00:22,521 --> 00:00:26,052
I put my sneakers beside hers and choose a pair of slippers.

12
00:00:26,052 --> 00:00:30,094
They have little clouds on them, which makes walking feel slightly more interesting.

13
00:00:30,314 --> 00:00:31,837
Make yourself comfortable.

14
00:00:31,837 --> 00:00:33,764
You can put your backpack by the chair.

15
00:00:34,036 --> 00:00:37,946
Her room has a shelf full of drawings and a desk covered with colored pencils.

16
00:00:37,946 --> 00:00:40,978
I reach toward a tiny clay cat, then stop.

17
00:00:40,978 --> 00:00:42,530
May I pick this up?

18
00:00:42,746 --> 00:00:43,331
Sure.

19
00:00:43,331 --> 00:00:44,602
Just hold the base.

20
00:00:44,602 --> 00:00:47,696
I made it in art class, and one ear is a little delicate.

21
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:50,265
I look at it carefully and put it back.

22
00:00:50,265 --> 00:00:53,161
We spend the afternoon drawing imaginary pets.

23
00:00:53,161 --> 00:00:55,620
Mine is a dog with enormous ears.

24
00:00:55,620 --> 00:00:58,370
Emma's is a very serious-looking purple turtle.

25
00:00:58,586 --> 00:00:59,994
Want to stay for a snack?

26
00:00:59,994 --> 00:01:01,682
My mom has sliced some fruit.

27
00:01:01,972 --> 00:01:03,497
That sounds great.

28
00:01:03,497 --> 00:01:08,028
Before Dad picks me up, I put the pencils away and leave the slippers by the basket.

29
00:01:08,028 --> 00:01:09,518
Thanks for having me.

30
00:01:09,746 --> 00:01:10,821
Come again soon.

31
00:01:10,821 --> 00:01:12,894
Your enormous-eared dog needs a friend.

32
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:15,590
Next time, I'll bring my sketchbook.

33
00:01:15,590 --> 00:01:19,288
The shoes can wait by the door while we invent another impossible animal.
